course: dictionary
lesson: 15158
title: Words for heat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scorched means burnt a little on the surface, turned brown or black by heat. Read the words around it to check. «The fire left the ground scorched and black.» Ground that is black after a fire has been burnt by the heat, so scorched fits.
explain: Scorched can also mean dried up by the hot sun. «The grass was scorched brown after three weeks without rain.» The clues are three weeks without rain and brown grass, so the sun has dried it up, like grass in a heatwave.
explain: Scorched is the past form of the verb scorch. Its other forms are scorch, scorches and scorching: «The sun is scorching the fields today.» The -ed ending tells you the heat has already happened.
fact: Scorched means burnt a little on the surface, turned brown or black by heat.
fact: Scorched also means dried up by the hot sun, like grass in a heatwave.
fact: «Scorched earth» is ground that has been burnt, often after a fire.
fact: «Sun-scorched» means damaged or dried up by strong sunshine.
fact: Scorched is the past form of the verb scorch: scorch, scorches, scorched, scorching.
exercise: «The fire left the ground scorched and black.» What does scorched mean here? | *Burnt a little on the surface, brown or black from heat | Cold and covered in snow | Bright and shiny like new | Wet and muddy after the rain
exercise: «The grass was scorched brown after three weeks without rain.» What dried the grass up? | Heavy rain | *The hot sun | A cold wind | A busy road
exercise: Which word is the past form of the verb scorch? | scorches | *scorched | scorching | scorch
test: «The bread was scorched on the bottom, so we scraped it off.» What does scorched show here? | *Burnt a little and turned brown from heat | Frozen solid in the freezer | Very tall and thin | Soaked with cold water
test: Which phrase is used for ground burnt by a big fire? | Wet mud | Clear blue sky | Soft sand | *Scorched earth
exam: Which word means dried up by the hot sun? | Soaked | Chilly | *Scorched | Frozen
